SUMMARY:The Saturday with Friends High Park Walk and Roncesvalles Polish F
 estival!
DESCRIPTION:Soul City Social Club (Toronto\, Canada)\nHello everyone\,\n\n
 **\\*\\*Please kindly read carefully- Thank you\\*\\***\n\nJoin us for a w
 onderful Saturday afternoon of walking\, conversation\, culture and new fr
 iendships! We’ll enjoy the natural beauty of **High Park** before contin
 uing to the lively **Roncesvalles Polish Festival\,** where the neighbourh
 ood comes alive with music\, entertainment\, food and community spirit.\nW
 hether you’re coming alone or bringing a friend\, you’ll be warmly wel
 comed. This is a relaxed social outing designed for people who enjoy explo
 ring Toronto\, meeting others and sharing good conversation along the way.
 \n\nWe will meet at **La Diperie Cafe** where you are welcome to grab a co
 ffee\, water\, pastry or ice cream if you like before we head out.\n\nThis
  will give us an opportunity to introduce ourselves as everyone arrives\; 
 then make our way on a friendly walk through the iconic **High Park in Tor
 onto.**\n\nEvent Details below:\n\nSincerely\,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Host/Or
 ganizer)\n\n**Event Details:**\n**The Saturday with Friends High Park Walk
  and Roncesvalles Polish Festival!**\n\nOur afternoon will begin with a le
 isurely walk through High Park\, one of Toronto’s most beautiful green s
 paces. We’ll stroll at a comfortable pace\, take in the scenery and have
  plenty of opportunities to talk and get to know one another.\n\nAfter our
  walk\, we’ll make our way toward Roncesvalles Avenue to experience the 
 Polish Festival. You can enjoy the festive atmosphere\, live entertainment
 \, cultural displays and a tempting variety of Polish food and treats.\n\n
 ###\n\n**Highlights:**\n\n* Take a relaxing and scenic walk through High P
 ark\n* Meet friendly people and make new connections\n* Explore the Ronces
 valles neighbourhood\n* Experience Polish music\, culture\, food and enter
 tainment\n* Enjoy a fun and welcoming Saturday afternoon in Toronto\n\nPle
 ase wear comfortable walking shoes and dress for the weather. Everyone is 
 responsible for purchasing their own food\, drinks and other items during 
 the festival.\nCome with a friendly attitude\, an open mind and a willingn
 ess to connect. Let’s walk\, laugh\, explore and enjoy a memorable Satur
 day together!\n\n**Event Fee:** 10 dollars when you arrive at the La Diper
 ie Cafe (cash only please)\nor e transfer in advance to **steveflemming11@
 gmail.com**\n\n\\*I strongly encourage you to take the subway as it is ver
 y close to the cafe but certainly driving in an option\n\\*Street parking 
 will be found along Bloor Street and residential area but not inside the p
 ark\n\n**Time and Location: Where to meet us?**\n(Please arrive on time :)
 \n\nMeet us at **La Diperie Cafe** at 2:30 p.m.\n(we will wait for everyon
 e until 3:00 p.m.)\n**Address:** 1960 Bloor St W\, Toronto\, ON M4W 1J2\nV
 ery close to the High Park Subway station\n(We will then head out for our 
 walk at that point)
